      "model": "claude-opus-5",
      "content": "## Files in `/path/to/projects/agent-harness`\n\n```\n.gitignore          bun.lock            package.json        tsconfig.json\nREADME.md           package-lock.json\n.opencode/          docs/               examples/           src/\ntests/              trials/  (untracked)\n```\n\n- `src/` — `adapters/` (claude, codex, gemini, kiro, opencode), `core/` (driver, normalize, pricing, store, types), `cli/` (harness.ts, lib.ts), `emitters/` (atif, otel), `monitors/` (transcripts, tmux-driver, kiro-mitm)\n- `docs/` — ARCHITECTURE.md, TOKEN-COUNTING.md\n- `examples/` — trial-all.sh, monitor-live.sh, emit-atif.ts\n- `tests/` — 12 test files plus `fixtures/` and `helpers/`\n\n## Summary\n\n- **What it is:** a headless-first orchestration and observability layer that wraps coding-agent CLIs (Claude Code, Codex CLI, OpenCode, Gemini CLI, Kiro) behind one adapter interface, so a single `harness run --agent X \"prompt\"` drives any of them via headless, ACP, or tmux lanes.\n\n- **What it produces:** a normalized event model with cache-aware token accounting and cost math (`core/pricing.ts` + `pricing-data.json`), exported as ATIF trajectory artifacts or OpenTelemetry `gen_ai` spans, plus per-agent state detection and live per-session token deltas via `harness watch`.\n\n- **Status/tooling:** TypeScript, v0.1.0, runs under both `tsx --test` and `bun test` on an identical suite (re-export shims deliberately banned to avoid skewed test counts); README flags `src/` as work-in-progress with open interface merges tracked in ARCHITECTURE.md §9. State persists in `~/.agent-harness`.",
